### Example MATLAB Code with Boundary Condition Checks

Let's consider the example of solving Laplace's equation with the boundary conditions:
- \( u(0,y) = 50 \) V
- \( u(2,y) = 0 \) V
- \( u(x,0) = 0 \) V
- \( u(x,2) = 0 \) V

Here is a MATLAB script that includes checks for the boundary conditions:

```matlab
% Define grid parameters
L = 2; % Length of the domain
Nx = 100; % Number of grid points in x direction
Ny = 100; % Number of grid points in y direction
hx = L / (Nx - 1); % Grid spacing in x direction
hy = L / (Ny - 1); % Grid spacing in y direction

% Initialize potential matrix
U = zeros(Ny, Nx);

% Boundary conditions
U(:, 1) = 50; % Left boundary
U(:, end) = 0; % Right boundary
U(1, :) = 0; % Bottom boundary
U(end, :) = 0; % Top boundary

% Debugging: Print boundary values
disp('Left boundary values:');
disp(U(:, 1));
disp('Right boundary values:');
disp(U(:, end));
disp('Bottom boundary values:');
disp(U(1, :));
disp('Top boundary values:');
disp(U(end, :));

% Iterative solver (Gauss-Seidel method)
tolerance = 1e-6;
max_iterations = 10000;
converged = false;
iterations = 0;

while ~converged && iterations < max_iterations
    U_old = U;
    for i = 2:Ny-1
        for j = 2:Nx-1
            U(i, j) = 0.25 * (U_old(i+1, j) + U_old(i-1, j) + U_old(i, j+1) + U_old(i, j-1));
        end
    end
    if norm(U - U_old, 'fro') / norm(U_old, 'fro') < tolerance
        converged = true;
    end
    iterations = iterations +  1;
end

% Plot the potential distribution
figure;
surf(U);
xlabel('x');
ylabel('y');
zlabel('Potential (V)');
title(['Potential Distribution with hx = ', num2str(hx), ' and hy = ', num2str(hy)]);
colorbar;
shading interp;
view(3);

% Print the value at (1,1)
fprintf('Potential at (1,1): %.2f V\n', U(round(Ny/2), round(Nx/2)));

