### Example Workflow in MATLAB

Here's a brief example of how you might set up a numerical solution in MATLAB:

```matlab
% Define parameters
L = 2; % Length of the beam
T_final = 1; % Final time
k = 0.2; % Thermal diffusivity
E = 200e9; % Young's modulus
q = 500; % Applied load

% Spatial discretization
Nx = 100;
x = linspace(0, L, Nx);
dx = x(2) - x(1);

% Time discretization
Nt = 1000;
dt = T_final / Nt;

% Initialize temperature and displacement
u = zeros(Nx, Nt+1);
v = zeros(Nx, Nx);

% Initial condition for temperature
u(:, 1) = 100 * sin(pi * x / 2);

% Boundary conditions for temperature
u(1, :) = 100;
u(end, :) = 50;

% Solve heat equation using finite difference method
for n = 1:Nt
    u(2:end-1, n+1) = u(2:end-1, n) + k * dt / dx^2 * (u(3:end, n) - 2*u(2:end-1, n) + u(1:end-2, n));
end

% Solve elastic deformation equation using finite difference method
for i = 2:Nx-1
    for j = 2:Nx-1
        v(i, j) = (v(i+1, j) + v(i-1, j) + v(i, j+1) + v(i, j-1) - (-q/E) * dx^2) / 4;
    end
end

% Plot results
figure;
plot(x, u(:, end));
title('Temperature Distribution at Final Time');
xlabel('Position (m)');
ylabel('Temperature (^\circ C)');

figure;
surf(x, x, v);
title('Displacement Distribution');
xlabel('Position (m)');
ylabel('Position (m)');
zlabel('Displacement (m)');
```

