### Step 2: Compute Heat Flux

Next, we'll compute the heat flux \( q \) using Fourier's law \( q = -k \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} \).

#### MATLAB Code for Heat Flux

```matlab
% Assume thermal conductivity k = 1 for simplicity
k = 1;

% Compute heat flux at the final time step
q = -k * diff(u(:, end)) / dx;

% Extend q to match the length of x
